{
  "_comment": "The default binding of @shexjs/neighborhood-wikibase's manifest vocabulary, stacked onto ../../doc/webapp-manifest-context.jsonld's core. An entry that names this neighborhood (neighborhood: wikibase, a core attribute) writes this backend's own parameters under one `wikibase:parms` mapping -- base, sitematrix, pages, cacheDir, bare inside it. This file only binds names: the wikibase: prefix and the wikibase:parms term, whose property-scoped @context (JSON-LD 1.1) is the file beside it, manifest-parms-context.jsonld, which expands those keys to wikibase: IRIs, so they can't collide with another backend's same-shaped attribute (compare neighborhood-sparql's own, differently-typed, endpoint). @protected, for the reason neighborhood-sparql's is: a clash with another stacked context is an error, not a silent override, and the scope file can be bound under another name. Tentative home, as with neighborhood-sparql: this reads Wikibase's own entity-page JSON, not anything ShEx-specific, so a wikidata- or Wikibase-tooling namespace may be a better long-term home for it.",

  "@context": {
    "@version": 1.1,
    "@protected": true,
    "wikibase": "http://shex.io/neighborhoods/wikibase#",

    "wikibase:parms": {
      "@id": "wikibase:parms",
      "@context": "manifest-parms-context.jsonld"
    }
  }
}
